GROUNDS
Article 17(1) entitles me to erasure without undue delay where, among other grounds:
- the data is no longer needed for the purpose it was collected for;
- I withdraw my consent and no other legal basis for the processing applies;
- I object to the processing and there are no overriding legitimate grounds; or
- the data has been processed unlawfully.

WHAT I ASK YOU TO DO
1. Delete all personal data about me from your databases.
2. Remove it from any data broker networks and partner sharing arrangements, and tell the recipients to do the same.
3. Confirm the deletion to me in writing.

Article 12(3) requires you to answer without undue delay and within one month of receiving this request. If you do not, I may complain to the competent supervisory authority.

